## Why This Is Asked

Assesses multi-account isolation, tenant tagging, and rapid containment capabilities in AWS.

## Key Concepts

- ABAC with aws:PrincipalTag
- SCPs and cross-account trust boundaries
- Tenant-scoped KMS keys with rotation
- PrivateLink/VPCE for data paths
- Immutable logging and breach-testing

## Code Example

```javascript
// trust policy snippet (conceptual)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole",
      "Resource": "*",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {"aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id": "${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}"}
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate breach containment within 60 seconds end-to-end?
- What telemetry would you rely on for incident attribution?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical understanding of mutual TLS in AWS, certificate lifecycle, and zero-trust patterns for multi-tenant serverless apps. It also probes how rotation, revocation, and test planning are integrated into day-1 security work.

## Key Concepts
- mutual TLS with API Gateway and ACM Private CA
- Lambda authorizer to extract tenant from client certificate and enforce least privilege
- Per-tenant IAM policies and fine-grained access controls
- Certificate revocation lists (CRL) stored centrally (S3 or DynamoDB) and checked at request time
- Certificate/CA rotation strategy and disruption-free rollout
- Test plan including revocation, logging, and incident response

## Code Example
```javascript
// Lambda authorizer skeleton: extract tenant from cert CN and build a policy
exports.handler = async (event) => {
  const cert = event.requestContext?.identity?.callerCert;
  const subjectCN = cert?.subject?.CN;
  const tenant = extractTenantFromCN(subjectCN); // custom parsing
  const policy = buildPolicy(tenant, event.methodArn);
  return policy;
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you revoke a single tenant cert and verify cross-resource denial without impacting other tenants?
- What are the trade-offs of using Lambda authorizers vs API Gateway JWT authorizers in this setup?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests cross-account access control using IAM roles, Secrets Manager, and KMS in a practical, beginner-friendly setup.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-account IAM role and trust policy
- Secrets Manager resource policy and rotation
- CMK policy and private connectivity via VPC endpoints
- Auditing with CloudTrail and Config

## Code Example
```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": "secretsmanager:GetSecretValue",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:secretsmanager:region:accountS:secret:NAME-*"
    }
  ]
}
```
```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole",
      "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::AccountS:role/LambdaRole"}
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you verify no privilege creep over time?
- What failure modes exist and how would you detect them?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical cross-account tenant isolation, serverless data flow, and incident response in a real-world AWS stack.

## Key Concepts
- ABAC with cross-account trust; per-tenant prefixes; pre-signed URLs; KMS rotation; logging; exfiltration controls; breach containment orchestration (Step Functions/EventBridge); multi-region auditing.

## Code Example
```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:PutObject"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::tenant-prefixes/*",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {"aws:RequestTag/tenant": "${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant}"}
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate that breach containment completes within 60 seconds? 
- What metrics and alarms would you surface to detect access drift?

Why This Is Asked
- Tests a practical, scalable multi-tenant pattern within a single bucket, emphasizing isolation, encryption, and rapid containment.
- Exercises policy design using S3, KMS, and IAM with MFA, plus a real-time breach response workflow.

Key Concepts
- Tenant isolation via per-tenant S3 prefix and IAM role scope
- SSE-KMS with per-tenant CMKs and encryption context validation
- Containment orchestration using EventBridge, Lambda, and CloudTrail

Code Example
```json
// S3 bucket policy (illustrative)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/Tenant123Role"},
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject","s3:PutObject"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::tenant-bucket/tenant-123/*",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {"s3:prefix": "tenant-123/"}
      }
    }
  ]
}
```
```json
// KMS key policy (illustrative)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/Tenant123Role"},
      "Action": ["kms:Encrypt","kms:Decrypt"],
      "Resource": "*",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {"kms:EncryptionContext:TenantID": "tenant-123"}
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the 60-second containment workflow end-to-end? 
- How would you extend this to support new tenants without increasing policy complexity?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to architect zero-trust, scalable cross-account access using ABAC and automated containment. Evaluates policy design, key management, and incident response integration.

## Key Concepts
- ABAC with Principal and Resource tags for cross-account trust
- AWS Organizations SCPs to strictly bound access
- Per-tenant KMS keys with rotation and strict key policies
- PrivateLink for service boundaries
- Security Hub/GuardDuty + EventBridge-driven containment
- Immutable multi-region CloudTrail audit trails

## Code Example
```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/TenantDataAccess",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "aws:PrincipalTag/tenant": "TenantA"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["kms:Encrypt","kms:Decrypt"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:kms:region:acct:key/tenant- TenantA-key",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "kms:ViaService": "s3.region.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would containment latency be tested and verified in production runs?
- What are pitfalls of ABAC at scale and how would you mitigate tag spoofing or tag mutation?
